[research] Read Common Risk Factors in Cryptocurrency (Liu, Tsyvinski, Wu, Journal of Finance 2022) (https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/jofi.13119) — Cryptocurrency market, size and momentum are the factors capturing cross-sectional expected returns; there is significant time-series momentum at daily and weekly frequencies and top past-return quintiles outperform bottom over 1-4 week horizons, strongest among larger coins (4.2% weekly for above-median size).; Risk Premia Harvesting Through Dual Momentum (Gary Antonacci, SSRN 2012) (https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=2042750) — Absolute momentum does far more than relative momentum to lessen volatility and drawdown; combining the two lets you keep relative momentum's returns while the absolute-momentum cash/bond switch cuts drawdown (39-year test: 17.43%/yr at 22.7% max drawdown vs 60.21% for the index).; Dual Momentum Trading Strategy — rules and backtest (QuantifiedStrategies) (https://www.quantifiedstrategies.com/dual-momentum-trading-strategy/) — Practitioner write-up of the mechanism: rank assets by relative strength, invest only when the pick's own absolute trailing return is positive, otherwise step aside to a safe asset — the switching rule that supplies the drawdown protection.
[hypothesis] Ranking the served crypto basket by ~60-day trailing return and holding the top 3 names ONLY while each clears a positive absolute-momentum gate (else cash) earns more than a fully-invested rotation net of costs and respects the 25% drawdown mandate, because absolute momentum moves the book to cash in broad downtrends; it is false if the gated top-3 underperforms buy-and-hold or breaches 25% drawdown in the 2026 forward window.
